        "heading": "Brittany Heitmann, LPCMH, NCC",
        "body": "<p>Brittany Heitmann is a Licensed Professional Counselor of Mental Health (LPCMH) with a strong foundation in clinical care and human services. She holds a Master’s degree in Clinical Mental Health, a Master’s degree in Human Services, and a Bachelor’s degree in Psychology.</p><p>Brittany specializes in family systems work and has extensive experience supporting families and individuals navigating trauma, grief, and communication challenges. Her approach is grounded in evidence-based practice and shaped by a deep respect for each client’s story, strengths, and values.</p><p>She has advanced training in Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT), Trauma-Focused Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (TF-CBT), and the Child and Family Traumatic Stress Intervention (CFTSI). Brittany believes that every person has a unique sense of purpose and a personal “why” that can guide meaningful change. Using a solution-focused approach, she partners with clients to develop practical, values-driven plans that support healing, growth, and lasting progress.</p>",
